    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 8.47,
      "end": 8.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Hi everyone. Welcome back."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 8.48,
      "end": 10.31,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "Okay, so in this problem, I'd like to"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.32,
      "end": 12.67,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "take a look at autonomous equations and"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 12.68,
      "end": 14.31,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "phase lines."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 14.32,
      "end": 15.47,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "And specifically, we're going to take a"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 15.48,
      "end": 17.27,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "look at this simple equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 17.28,
      "end": 19.91,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "x. = ax + 1"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 19.92,
      "end": 22.43,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "which models births and death rates and"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 22.44,
      "end": 24.07,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "a fixed replenishment rate for a"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 24.08,
      "end": 25.99,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "population."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 26.0,
      "end": 28.75,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "So, in this case, uh the the variable A"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 28.76,
      "end": 30.03,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "represents"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 30.04,
      "end": 32.63,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "births minus deaths"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 32.64,
      "end": 35.59,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "in a population and one represents the"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 35.6,
      "end": 39.95,
      "duration": 4.35,
      "text": "constant input of uh new creatures."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 39.96,
      "end": 42.51,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "Okay, so for part A, we're asked to find"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 42.52,
      "end": 45.03,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "intervals of the variable A"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 45.04,
      "end": 46.39,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "uh which determine the long-time"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 46.4,
      "end": 47.75,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "stability"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 47.76,
      "end": 50.39,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "of uh the population."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 50.4,
      "end": 53.43,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "And then secondly for each uh one or for"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 53.44,
      "end": 55.99,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "each typical case of A in"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 56.0,
      "end": 57.75,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "in the first part of the problem we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 57.76,
      "end": 60.31,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "asked to sketch a phase line"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 60.32,
      "end": 62.27,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "and then also to sketch the solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 62.28,
      "end": 65.11,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "x(t) versus t."
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 65.12,
      "end": 66.75,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "Okay, so I'll let you take a look at"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 66.76,
      "end": 68.19,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "this problem and I'll be back in a"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 68.2,
      "end": 83.75,
      "duration": 15.55,
      "text": "moment."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 86.03,
      "end": 86.04,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Hi everyone. Welcome back."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 86.04,
      "end": 86.91,
      "duration": 0.87,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 86.92,
      "end": 89.11,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "So, the problem we're uh looking at is"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 89.12,
      "end": 96.87,
      "duration": 7.75,
      "text": "x. = ax."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 98.31,
      "end": 98.32,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And as mentioned in the title of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 98.32,
      "end": 100.39,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "problem uh this is an autonomous"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 100.4,
      "end": 102.27,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "equation which means that the right-hand"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 102.28,
      "end": 104.23,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "side is not a function of time. The"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 104.24,
      "end": 107.19,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "right-hand side only depends on x."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 107.2,
      "end": 109.35,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "And for these types of problems"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 109.36,
      "end": 110.11,
      "duration": 0.75,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 110.12,
      "end": 112.27,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "the the critical points or the place"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 112.28,
      "end": 114.03,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "that the points at which the right-hand"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 114.04,
      "end": 115.31,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "side vanish"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 115.32,
      "end": 116.63,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "tend to determine the long-time"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 116.64,
      "end": 119.43,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "characteristics of the solution."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 119.44,
      "end": 121.51,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "So, we can kind of get a handle on what"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 121.52,
      "end": 123.67,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "intervals of A uh determine the"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 123.68,
      "end": 127.87,
      "duration": 4.19,
      "text": "long-time stability"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 136.27,
      "end": 136.28,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "what x. versus x might look like."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 136.28,
      "end": 139.03,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "And we see that if A is positive"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 139.04,
      "end": 147.91,
      "duration": 8.87,
      "text": "this represents a line"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 160.83,
      "end": 160.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "of the intercept uh with the x-axis"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 160.84,
      "end": 164.67,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "uh x. is positive"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 164.68,
      "end": 165.95,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "which means"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 165.96,
      "end": 167.43,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "that"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 167.44,
      "end": 170.47,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "uh when the line goes through the"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 170.48,
      "end": 173.75,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "the point y uh x. = 0"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 173.76,
      "end": 176.31,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "uh the term ax + 1 is going to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 176.32,
      "end": 182.51,
      "duration": 6.19,
      "text": "positive."
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 183.87,
      "end": 183.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "I'll just point out that this point"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 183.88,
      "end": 185.31,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "right here"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 185.32,
      "end": 188.67,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "is when x. is equal to zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 188.68,
      "end": 190.27,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "and this happens when x is equal to"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 190.28,
      "end": 192.11,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "negative"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 192.12,
      "end": 193.99,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "1 over A."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 194.0,
      "end": 195.75,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "So, this point right here is"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 195.76,
      "end": 197.27,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "negative"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 197.28,
      "end": 203.55,
      "duration": 6.27,
      "text": "1 over A."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 206.63,
      "end": 206.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And when x is below negative 1 over A"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 206.64,
      "end": 209.15,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "x. is negative which means that"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 209.16,
      "end": 210.67,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "solutions will want to move away from"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 210.68,
      "end": 218.71,
      "duration": 8.03,
      "text": "the point negative 1 over A."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 220.31,
      "end": 220.32,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "What other qualitative behavior could we"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 220.32,
      "end": 221.23,
      "duration": 0.91,
      "text": "have?"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 221.24,
      "end": 223.31,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "Well, when A is below zero, when A is"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 223.32,
      "end": 227.47,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "less than zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 228.87,
      "end": 228.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "the slope of this curve is going to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 228.88,
      "end": 231.07,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "negative."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 231.08,
      "end": 236.99,
      "duration": 5.91,
      "text": "So, I'll plot again x. versus x."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 238.39,
      "end": 238.4,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And again, the intercept is going to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 238.4,
      "end": 244.07,
      "duration": 5.67,
      "text": "at negative 1 over A."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 245.87,
      "end": 245.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "However, when x is above the critical"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 245.88,
      "end": 247.95,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "point"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 247.96,
      "end": 249.91,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "x. is negative"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 249.92,
      "end": 251.71,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "so solutions will want to tend to move"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 251.72,
      "end": 255.23,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "back towards negative 1 over A."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 255.24,
      "end": 257.31,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "And when x is below the critical point,"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 257.32,
      "end": 261.47,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "we see that x. is in the upper plane"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 261.48,
      "end": 263.39,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "which means it's positive, so solutions"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 263.4,
      "end": 267.07,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "will want to grow."
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 269.35,
      "end": 269.36,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, we have two cases right now."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 269.36,
      "end": 271.75,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "One is when A is bigger than zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 271.76,
      "end": 274.19,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "One is when A is less than zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 274.2,
      "end": 275.27,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "And then of course, there's going to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 275.28,
      "end": 279.83,
      "duration": 4.55,
      "text": "an intermediar intermediate point"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 282.75,
      "end": 282.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "which is when A A is equal to zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 282.76,
      "end": 287.11,
      "duration": 4.35,
      "text": "And in this case"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 288.91,
      "end": 288.92,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "the curve x."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 288.92,
      "end": 296.19,
      "duration": 7.27,
      "text": "versus x"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 299.31,
      "end": 299.32,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "is just going to be a straight line"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 299.32,
      "end": 303.75,
      "duration": 4.43,
      "text": "that goes through one."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 306.59,
      "end": 306.6,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, so this gives us three regions uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 306.6,
      "end": 307.19,
      "duration": 0.59,
      "text": "that"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 307.2,
      "end": 309.39,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "that are will determine the long-time uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 309.4,
      "end": 310.83,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "behavior."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 310.84,
      "end": 313.15,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "So, the three regions are"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 313.16,
      "end": 315.27,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "A equals zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 315.28,
      "end": 317.35,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "A less than zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 317.36,
      "end": 320.55,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "and then A bigger than zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 320.56,
      "end": 323.15,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "Okay, so this concludes part A."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 323.16,
      "end": 324.35,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "And for part B, we're asked to"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 324.36,
      "end": 326.79,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "investigate the behavior of"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 326.8,
      "end": 328.75,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "each of these three regions"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 328.76,
      "end": 329.31,
      "duration": 0.55,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 329.32,
      "end": 332.15,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "by constructing a phase line and then"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 332.16,
      "end": 333.83,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "secondly, by sketching a solution or"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 333.84,
      "end": 337.03,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "several solutions."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 346.47,
      "end": 346.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "let's take a look at the case when A is"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 346.48,
      "end": 348.63,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "bigger than zero first."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 348.64,
      "end": 350.03,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "And I'm just going to pick one value of"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 350.04,
      "end": 351.19,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "A."
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 351.2,
      "end": 355.31,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "I'll just pick A is equal to one"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 361.63,
      "end": 361.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And we're asked to sketch a phase line."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 361.64,
      "end": 365.95,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "So, I'll plot the phase line x here."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 367.47,
      "end": 367.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And we know from the ODE that the"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 367.48,
      "end": 369.71,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "critical point occurs at negative 1 over"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 369.72,
      "end": 370.83,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "A."
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 370.84,
      "end": 372.15,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "So, in this case, the there's going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 372.16,
      "end": 374.43,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "be one critical point"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 374.44,
      "end": 378.63,
      "duration": 4.19,
      "text": "and it's going to be at negative one."
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 381.31,
      "end": 381.32,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Now, when x is bigger than negative one"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 381.32,
      "end": 383.71,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "we've already seen that the arrows"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 383.72,
      "end": 384.39,
      "duration": 0.67,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 384.4,
      "end": 387.39,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "or that x. is going to be positive."
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 387.4,
      "end": 388.75,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "So, when"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 388.76,
      "end": 391.23,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "when x is bigger than negative one"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 391.24,
      "end": 394.95,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "in this region, x. is positive."
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 394.96,
      "end": 398.47,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "So, above negative one, x. is positive"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 398.48,
      "end": 401.23,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "which means that if a solution starts at"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 401.24,
      "end": 404.23,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "a point above negative one"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 404.24,
      "end": 406.75,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "it's going to constantly increase"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 406.76,
      "end": 408.75,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "forever."
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 408.76,
      "end": 410.19,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "And likewise, if it's below negative"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 410.2,
      "end": 413.91,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "one, it's going to decrease forever."
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 413.92,
      "end": 416.51,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "So, this is x. is negative in this"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 416.52,
      "end": 418.11,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "region."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 418.12,
      "end": 419.47,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "And of course"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 419.48,
      "end": 422.43,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "uh x. is zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 422.44,
      "end": 426.67,
      "duration": 4.23,
      "text": "at the critical point."
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 428.15,
      "end": 428.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Which means if we start at the critical"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 428.16,
      "end": 430.83,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "point, we stay there for all time."
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 430.84,
      "end": 435.11,
      "duration": 4.27,
      "text": "Okay, so let's sketch some solutions."
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 436.47,
      "end": 436.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 436.48,
      "end": 437.99,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "whenever I have"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 438.0,
      "end": 438.71,
      "duration": 0.71,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 438.72,
      "end": 440.19,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "whenever I have to sketch solutions for"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 440.2,
      "end": 441.47,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "a phase plane"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 441.48,
      "end": 443.79,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "or for a phase line"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 443.8,
      "end": 445.43,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "the first solution I always plot is"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 445.44,
      "end": 447.91,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "going to be the critical point."
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 447.92,
      "end": 450.39,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "So, note that x = -1 solves the"
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 450.4,
      "end": 452.23,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "differential equation. So, x equals a"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 452.24,
      "end": 453.51,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "critical point always solves the"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 453.52,
      "end": 455.43,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "differential equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 455.44,
      "end": 458.63,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "So, that means"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 461.63,
      "end": 461.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "uh when x is equal to negative one"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 461.64,
      "end": 465.95,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "we solve the differential equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 470.11,
      "end": 470.12,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "When x is bigger than negative one"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 470.12,
      "end": 478.55,
      "duration": 8.43,
      "text": "we obtain exponential growth."
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 480.47,
      "end": 480.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And when x is less than negative one, we"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 480.48,
      "end": 482.47,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "have exponential growth in the opposite"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 482.48,
      "end": 484.99,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 485.0,
      "end": 486.95,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "So, this is sometimes said to be an"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 486.96,
      "end": 490.23,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "unstable uh critical point because any"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 490.24,
      "end": 491.87,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "small perturbation away from negative"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 491.88,
      "end": 495.15,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "one will make the solution diverge."
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 495.16,
      "end": 497.87,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "Also note that each one of these curves"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 497.88,
      "end": 499.75,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "or once I have one of these curves, I"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 499.76,
      "end": 501.95,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "can generate all the others by just"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 501.96,
      "end": 504.07,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "picking it up and shifting it over."
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 504.08,
      "end": 507.23,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "And the reason this this works"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 507.24,
      "end": 508.67,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "is because the original equation is"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 508.68,
      "end": 510.39,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "autonomous, meaning that the right-hand"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 510.4,
      "end": 513.11,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "side didn't depend on time."
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 513.12,
      "end": 514.23,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "So, whenever you have an autonomous"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 514.24,
      "end": 515.39,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 515.4,
      "end": 516.75,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "when you sketch one solution, you can"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 516.76,
      "end": 518.909,
      "duration": 2.149,
      "text": "always get the others by just picking or"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 518.919,
      "end": 520.589,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "you can always get a family of others by"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 520.599,
      "end": 521.83,
      "duration": 1.231,
      "text": "picking up that solution and just"
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 521.84,
      "end": 522.95,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "shifting it to the right and to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 522.96,
      "end": 530.19,
      "duration": 7.23,
      "text": "left."
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 535.83,
      "end": 535.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "uh or when A is below zero, I'll just"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 535.84,
      "end": 541.15,
      "duration": 5.31,
      "text": "pick the value of A equals negative one."
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 544.79,
      "end": 544.8,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "We have a critical point at one."
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 544.8,
      "end": 546.55,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "And in this case, the arrows are going"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 546.56,
      "end": 549.27,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "to point towards one"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 549.28,
      "end": 555.47,
      "duration": 6.19,
      "text": "like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 557.95,
      "end": 557.96,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And again, I can sketch some"
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 557.96,
      "end": 559.43,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "curves."
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 559.44,
      "end": 569.11,
      "duration": 9.67,
      "text": "So, I'll first draw the solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 571.63,
      "end": 571.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "when x is equal to one."
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 571.64,
      "end": 575.23,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "And in this case"
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 578.63,
      "end": 578.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "solutions are going to converge"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 578.64,
      "end": 584.35,
      "duration": 5.71,
      "text": "towards the critical point."
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 586.43,
      "end": 586.44,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And in this case, we say that the"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 586.44,
      "end": 589.03,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "critical point x = 1"
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 589.04,
      "end": 594.39,
      "duration": 5.35,
      "text": "is stable."
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 595.55,
      "end": 595.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And that's because any small"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 595.56,
      "end": 599.19,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "perturbation"
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 600.15,
      "end": 600.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 600.16,
      "end": 601.75,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "makes the solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 601.76,
      "end": 602.47,
      "duration": 0.71,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 602.48,
      "end": 604.35,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "come back. Any small perturbation in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 604.36,
      "end": 605.55,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 605.56,
      "end": 607.23,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "will eventually just come back to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 607.24,
      "end": 610.83,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "critical point at x = 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 612.91,
      "end": 612.92,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay. And now lastly,"
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 612.92,
      "end": 614.83,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "we have the third case,"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 614.84,
      "end": 619.51,
      "duration": 4.67,
      "text": "which is when a equals zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 621.07,
      "end": 621.08,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And in this case, there are no critical"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 621.08,
      "end": 625.27,
      "duration": 4.19,
      "text": "points. In fact, x dot was equal to 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 625.28,
      "end": 629.07,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "So, x dot is positive"
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 630.83,
      "end": 630.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "for all values of x."
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 630.84,
      "end": 632.95,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "So, our phase line is just a line with"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 632.96,
      "end": 634.87,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "arrows."
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 634.88,
      "end": 636.79,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "And in this case, if I was if I were to"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 636.8,
      "end": 639.31,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "sketch some solutions,"
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 639.32,
      "end": 642.71,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "I'll just draw my axes."
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 644.07,
      "end": 644.08,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "x and t."
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 644.08,
      "end": 645.87,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "There are no critical points."
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 645.88,
      "end": 648.11,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "x is just increasing."
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 648.12,
      "end": 649.75,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "So, the solutions are going to look"
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 649.76,
      "end": 653.63,
      "duration": 3.87,
      "text": "something like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 656.19,
      "end": 656.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "They're just going to be straight lines."
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 656.2,
      "end": 660.79,
      "duration": 4.59,
      "text": "A family of straight lines."
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 662.43,
      "end": 662.44,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 662.44,
      "end": 663.63,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "So, we've just sketched some phase"
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 663.64,
      "end": 665.67,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "lines, and we sketched several solutions"
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 665.68,
      "end": 667.51,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "for each phase line. We've seen how the"
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 667.52,
      "end": 668.95,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "critical points"
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 668.96,
      "end": 669.51,
      "duration": 0.55,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 669.52,
      "end": 670.99,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "and the the arrows around the critical"
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 671.0,
      "end": 673.27,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "points affect the long-time behavior of"
    },
    {
      "index": 244,
      "start": 673.28,
      "end": 675.07,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "the solutions."
    },
    {
      "index": 245,
      "start": 675.08,
      "end": 678.03,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "And uh this is typically the process uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 246,
      "start": 678.04,
      "end": 680.03,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "that you uh go through when looking at"
    },
    {
      "index": 247,
      "start": 680.04,
      "end": 682.829,
      "duration": 2.789,
      "text": "autonomous equations."
    },
    {
      "index": 248,
      "start": 682.839,
      "end": 684.47,
      "duration": 1.631,
      "text": "You always first A, find the critical"
    },
    {
      "index": 249,
      "start": 684.48,
      "end": 685.75,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "points."
    },
    {
      "index": 250,
      "start": 685.76,
      "end": 687.39,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "Then B, find the regions between the"
    },
    {
      "index": 251,
      "start": 687.4,
      "end": 689.07,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "critical points and figure out if x dot"
    },
    {
      "index": 252,
      "start": 689.08,
      "end": 692.07,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "is either positive or negative."
    },
    {
      "index": 253,
      "start": 692.08,
      "end": 693.67,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "And then that that automatically gives"
    },
    {
      "index": 254,
      "start": 693.68,
      "end": 695.91,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "you the phase line."
    },
    {
      "index": 255,
      "start": 695.92,
      "end": 697.43,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "Once you have the phase line, you can"
    },
    {
      "index": 256,
      "start": 697.44,
      "end": 698.71,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "always just sketch a family of"
    },
    {
      "index": 257,
      "start": 698.72,
      "end": 700.51,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "solutions."
    },
    {
      "index": 258,
      "start": 700.52,
      "end": 702.71,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "Okay. So, I'd like to conclude here, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 259,
      "start": 702.72,
      "end": 705.52,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "I'll see you next time."
    }
  ],
